Alembic migration environment for the backend database.

The database URL is read from backend/.env through app.config. A process-level
DATABASE_URL environment variable takes precedence.

Run migrations from the backend directory:

    python -m alembic upgrade head

Inspect the current revision:

    python -m alembic current

Create a future migration after changing app/models.py:

    python -m alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe the schema change"

This repository adopted Alembic after the base schema already existed. The
first revision manages the R3 table only. For a brand-new database, initialize
the base tables once before recording the Alembic revision:

    python -c "from app.db import init_db; init_db()"
    python -m alembic upgrade head

The first revision inspects the live schema so that databases previously
initialized by create_all() can be adopted safely. It must be run online;
`alembic upgrade head --sql` is intentionally unsupported.

Back up a production database before upgrading. Downgrade is intentionally
blocked because this revision may adopt an existing R3 table with historical
analysis data; blindly dropping that table would cause data loss.
